 #:seon.task{:name "edn-symbol-text-accepts-a-leading-slash",
            :intent
            "`seon.program/edn-symbol-text?` answers true for symbol text that clojure's EDN reader refuses when the text starts with a slash and holds a second one, e.g. \"//.\", \"//|\", \"/?/?\" and \"/'//\" (differential against `clojure.edn/read-string` over 20,000 random strings on default, 4 mismatches, all of this class). Its docstring promises \"reads as one symbol token\", and the reader's pattern allows a leading slash only for the whole text \"/\". Correct: `seon.program/edn-symbol-text?` is true for a slash-led text only when the text is exactly \"/\"; every other answer stays as it is. `seon.program/edn-round-trip-symbol?` masks the defect today for symbols (it also tests the namespace split), so the proof calls the private function.",
            :must-read #{seon.program/edn-symbol-text? seon.program/edn-round-trip-symbol?}}
 #:seon.task{:name "cluster-attributes-are-the-declared-cluster-entities"
             :intent "Phase AW0 of the evidence. A third value of `:seon.program/partition`, `:seon.cluster`, marks the entities whose facts an attempt's successful end copies onto main: `seon.task/task`, `seon.task/assignment-row` and `seon.error.occurrence/occurrence` declare it, with one rule on the entity schema, `:seon.cluster/conflict` (:root default, a problem task for root; :theirs; :ours; :add on the occurrence count). Messages are not cluster facts: they travel on the recipient's inbox channel and are written by the recipient on its own branch (:seon.data). `seon.program/cluster-attributes` derives the attributes from the projection as `seon.program/program-attributes` does (same projection-cache-value pattern) and answers the rule per attribute; `seon.schema`'s partition check accepts `:seon.cluster` and requires an identity attribute for it (the copy matches by identity, never entity id). Vocabulary rows (cherry-pick, :seon.cluster, end copy, inbox) land first. Proof: this test on the packaged projection: cluster-attributes contains :seon.task.attempt/end, :seon.task/intent and :seon.error.occurrence/count, excludes :seon.message/to and is disjoint from program-attributes; a fixture :seon.cluster schema with no identity refuses with :seon.schema/member :seon.db/identity; derivation under 5 ms warm. Platform slice (--test). Files: resources/seon/schemas/seon.task.edn, seon.error.occurrence.edn, src/seon/program.cljc, src/seon/schema.clj, the evidence, test/seon/program_test.clj."
             :must-read #{seon.program/program-attributes seon.schema/build-projection seon.db/identity-attributes}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-11/hybrid-agent-world.md"
